## [:< ##

# name  = base.path-template.zenka-symlink-chain
# descr = zenka name and launcher context resolved from a symlink chain
# param = [ link_path ]

##  walks a launcher link through the filesystem symlink chain until a       ##
##  recognized name form terminates it [ see                                 ##
##  <[path-template.zenka-name-from-link]> ] or a real file ends it,         ##
##  collecting every name walked on the way :                                ##
##                                                                          ##
##      {   zenka_name => 'radio',                                          ##
##          chain      => [ 'radio-jazz', 'p7-radio' ],                     ##
##          launcher   => [ 'radio-jazz' ],                                 ##
##          target     => undef,                                            ##
##          source     => 'symlink-chain'  }                                ##
##                                                                          ##
##  'chain' holds every basename walked, in order.  'launcher' holds all of  ##
##  them but the last -- the last one either named the zenka or is the       ##
##  interpreter binary the chain ended in, so the rest is launcher-preset    ##
##  context for the zenka that got started.  'source' is one of              ##
##  'program-name', 'symlink-chain' or 'argv'                                ##
##                                                                          ##
##  without a parameter this reports the resolution of the running process'  ##
##  own invocation, resolved once at start-up and also available as          ##
##  <system.start.symlink_chain> / <system.start.launcher_chain>             ##

## the bootstrap implementation lives in bin/Protocol-7, because zenka-name ##
## resolution runs before the module system is live -- this registry entry  ##
## publishes it under the canonical 'path-template.*' name so zenka code    ##
## never reaches for the interpreter-local one  [ see                       ##
## data/md/design/ZENKA-SYMLINK-CHAIN-RESOLUTION.md ]                       ##

return <[base.resolve_zenka_symlink_chain]>->(@ARG);

